        </ul>

        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            A small, sound, flat driveway is a DIY job: 100 to 150 dollars, a Saturday, two full coats after real prep in the right weather, and a result that will last two to three years. A large, cracked, sloped or oxidised one is a professional job, because hot crack fill and a sand-loaded commercial mix are the things that will make it last, and you cannot buy them at retail.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Whichever way you go, the failure mode is the same: skipped prep, a thin coat and bad timing. A careful homeowner beats a careless contractor every time. A good contractor beats both.
          </p>
        </div>

